On 02/07/2015 14:20, Erik Natanael Gustafsson wrote:
>
>     That means "all the birds join in the same [as something else]
>     song". If you
>     mean "same [as each other]", you can say "mitsi'u", or reword it,
>     "ro loi
>     cipni cu mitsi'u lo ka ce'u sanga makau".
>
> Ahh, good. I'll simply change it to mitsi'u then. Out of curiosity,=20
> could one shorten your alternative to "ro loi cipni cu mitsi'u lo ka=20
> sanga" having the other places implicit without losing to much meaning?
I would say {lo ro cipni cu dunsi'u lo ka sanga}, here. I don't think=20
{ro loi cipni cu simxu...} is correct here, because this {ro} makes it=20
distributive, whereas {simxu} expects a plurality of individuals.

As a side note, you can move around the sentence elements for achieving=20
better rhymes.

>
>     > .i loi melbi selpeisku po do cu rivli'a se ka'a lo sasfoi .ijebo
>     mi'o bajra
>     > gi'e farlu gi'e sa'irbi'o je refcfa bajra .i mi'o bajra mu'i lo
>     ricfoi
>     > .ijebo mi'o bajra mu'i lo ka ro da na'e claxu lo selfi'a
>
>     "sa'irbi'o je refcfa" modifies "bajra". I'm not sure that's what
>     you mean.
>
> Ahh, okay. No, the reason I didn't use gi'e between "sa'irbi'o" and=20
> "refcfa bajra" was that I wanted to group them more together than with=20
> the previous selbri, but perhaps that isn't necessary. Changing je to=20
> gi'e would fix it right? Is there another way of grouping selbri=20
> without creating tanru?

Tighter grouping is achieved with {bo}. For example, {brode gi'e bo=20
brodo}. You can also opt for {gi'e ba bo}, which means "and then=E2=80=A6" =
(gi'e=20
in itself has no implication of temporal sequence, although a temporal=20
sequence may be deduced from context; for making a temporal sequence of=20
events explicit, you can use {gi'e ba bo}).

By the way, {selpeisku} is undefined. Why not using simply {se peisku},=20
or {se pensi}? Also, using {po} there is a little weird (if I'm not=20
mistaken, {po} is for social/legal possessions). {lo se peisku pe do} or=20
{lo se peisku be do} would fit better I think. ({be} is for if {do} is=20
the one who thinks the thought we're talking about; {pe} is for if the=20
thought are related to {do}, without specifying if {do} is the one who=20
think them).

mi'e la .ilmen. mu'o


